s/in-1888-wisconsin-publisher-and-womens-rights-pioneer-lisle-lester-died-penniless-in-new-york-her-ashes-went-unclaimed-for-138-years-and-are-finally-returning-home-to-fond-du-lac/articleshow/133833661.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T17:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133834215,imgsize-78546.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Kentucky protected a vast elk landscape]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133835968.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Kentucky hunters faced uncertainty with temporary land access agreements. A new conservation partnership secured permanent public access to a large elk hunting area. This agreement provides 54,560 acres for public use in eastern Kentucky. The project involved state officials, conservation groups, and federal funding programs. This ensures continued hunting traditions and habitat restoration for future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kentucky-hunters-were-stuck-with-an-agreement-that-landowners-could-cancel-in-30-days-a-54560-acre-easement-now-permanently-keeps-a-huge-elk-landscape-open-in-a-state-where-95-of-land-is-private/articleshow/133835968.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kentucky-hunters-were-stuck-with-an-agreement-that-landowners-could-cancel-in-30-days-a-54560-acre-easement-now-permanently-keeps-a-huge-elk-landscape-open-in-a-state-where-95-of-land-is-private/articleshow/133835968.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T17:17:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133836136,imgsize-340230.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Banking on the dollar: How 