/&gt;<![CDATA[In 2024, Jeff and Betsy Yingling bought 101 acres in Freedom Township, Adams County, Pennsylvania, and soon began considering how to protect the land permanently. After living there and seeing its wildlife, cropland, wooded areas and changing scenery, they decided to place a preservation easement on the property. The easement was finalised in August 2026, permanently protecting all 101 acres for future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-a-pennsylvania-couple-bought-101-acres-near-their-hometown-before-the-sale-was-even-final-they-began-planning-to-protect-it-and-in-2026-all-101-acres-were-permanently-preserved/articleshow/133829776.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2024-a-pennsylvania-couple-bought-101-acres-near-their-hometown-before-the-sale-was-even-final-they-began-planning-to-protect-it-and-in-2026-all-101-acres-were-permanently-preserved/articleshow/133829776.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T14:21:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133831468,imgsize-1057605.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Seattle light rail linked to deaths of 2,000 fish in Lake Washington five months after opening]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133798363.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/seattle-opened-light-rail-across-the-i-90-floating-bridge-in-march-five-months-later-about-2000-fish-have-died-near-electrical-equipment-hanging-into-lake-washington/articleshow/133798363.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/seattle-opened-light-rail-across-the-i-90-floating-bridge-in-march-five-months-later-about-2000-fish-have-died-near-electrical-equipment-hanging-into-lake-washington/articleshow/133798363.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T15:28:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133798542,imgsize-183009.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[242 trapped by wildfire; pilots flew into flames to save them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133832449.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[California National Guard crews performed a historic nighttime helicopter rescue during the Creek Fire.  They saved 242 people trapped by intense flames and thick smoke.  This extraordinary mission utilized night-vision goggles and combat helicopters in a wildfire zone.  The daring rescue demonstrated new possibilities for nighttime wildfire aviation response.  California has since expanded its nighttime aviation capabilities and interagency training.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-smoke-forced-civilian-aircraft-out-of-the-sky-with-242-people-trapped-by-californias-creek-fire-calguard-crews-flew-into-the-flames-at-night-in-the-largest-helicopter-rescue-in-national-guard-history-and-saved-all-of-them-in-seven-hours/articleshow/133832449.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-smoke-forced-civilian-aircraft-out-of-the-sky-with-242-people-trapped-by-californias-creek-fire-calguard-crews-flew-into-the-flames-at-night-in-the-largest-helicopter-rescue-in-national-guard-history-and-saved-all-of-them-in-seven-hours/articleshow/133832449.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T15:15:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133832671,imgsize-427413.cms"/></item></channel></rss>